{"game": "redfall", "language": "english", "appid": 1294810, "month": "2025-02", "window": 1, "start_date": 1738368000, "end_date": 1740787199, "month_true_total": 14, "quota": 14, "returned": 14, "pulled_at": "2026-09-02 17:06:25 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "188853646", "author": {"steamid": "76561198867124556", "personaname": "whiskey", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/ggwhiskey/", "num_games_owned": 1619, "num_reviews": 524, "playtime_forever": 428, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 428, "last_played": 1740471525, "avatar": "840c3970f5b4c73c0f2038d910c4e75263de622b"}, "language": "english", "review": "[h1][b]A Vampire Game That Sucks… But Not in a Good Way[/b][/h1]\n\nI went into Redfall hoping for at least a decent co-op shooter, but what I got instead was one of the most shockingly bad AAA releases in recent years. This game is an absolute disaster on almost every level, and the negative reviews are 100% deserved.\n\nThe control doesn't feel great a t all, the movement feels stiff and floaty. It just neve feels satisfying to play. \n\nThe plot had potential, but it was executed terribly. Vampires taking over a town sounds pretty cool imo! But the way we were presented with the story is laughably bad. The story is completely forgettable, and by the time you get through the missions, you won’t care about anything that’s happening.\n\nAnother thing is, there are no proper cutscenes! Instead all we get are [b]PowerPoint slides[/b]. Seriously a really baffling choice. Instead of actual cutscenes, Redfall presents its major story moments through still images with no animation whatsoever. Imagine paying full price for a game these days, only to get something that looks like a slideshow instead of a cinematic experience. It feels lazy and completely kills any sense of immersion.\n\nFor a game released at AAA pricing, Redfall gives you the bare minimum of effort. This game simply not worth your time or money.\n", "timestamp_created": 1740648403, "timestamp_updated": 1740648403, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 59, "votes_funny": 12, "weighted_vote_score": "0.788314461708068848", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1682985798", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 17, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 13, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 5, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 6, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "188797996", "author": {"steamid": "76561198303470849", "personaname": "Bumberclatt-Swagツ", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198303470849/", "num_games_owned": 556, "num_reviews": 63, "playtime_forever": 1527, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1527, "last_played": 1740580012, "avatar": "c44b5b8c842bfe382e0661106d15f8a98fe6dc26"}, "language": "english", "review": "It's actually not that bad, however you have to be prepared to play through it on the hardest difficulty in order to experience any sort of challenge. Redfall was made during the pandemic which is really evident in the final product (You can literally pick up and sell toilet paper). The story is ok and the guns all feel nice to shoot, the open world is filled with people to rescue (which earns you points to level up a totally different skill tree) and unique weapons which I enjoyed hunting! Overall, I'd give it a 7/10", "timestamp_created": 1740580221, "timestamp_updated": 1740580221, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 6, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.487203806638717651", "comment_count": 2, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1682985798", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "188265887", "author": {"steamid": "76561198130824164", "personaname": "ModernWarMEXICN", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198130824164/", "num_games_owned": 1220, "num_reviews": 143, "playtime_forever": 1166, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1166, "deck_playtime_at_review": 1166, "last_played": 1739967596, "avatar": "597c6209776035285c742e3cf3b71e7ffb754fa6"}, "language": "english", "review": "Let me be clear, This gets a negative review because i ran into a game breaking bug. For the first time ever in my gaming career mind you. That made me lose nearly 20 hours of progress and i literally cant advance the story cause one of the main missions bugged and i cant finish the objective. If you like farcry style games this one is fine. Just very rpg heavy and frankly doesn't need it. The world is rather empty and the AI is certainly on the spectrum. The story and characters are so ugh i literally skipped all the cutscenes. The games art style directly impedes its attempt at a serious tone. The Main character's boil down to an Indian who thinks hes funny and quirky but just annoying, the tech girl whos forgettable as she is generic, the shoehorned black woman and a guy whos already like half vampire. the weapons are basic af and nothing about it stands out its just a game that again if you like farcry can get into this. Im not one to abandon games but im not restarting after being like half way through the game. Otherwise i would've maybe given the game a positive review", "timestamp_created": 1739968812, "timestamp_updated": 1739968812, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.494756191968917847", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": true, "app_release_date": "1682985798", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "188180162", "author": {"steamid": "76561198037108662", "personaname": "Foat", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198037108662/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 320, "playtime_forever": 1290, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 458, "last_played": 1740795117, "avatar": "dd7c2b8cd9ac844b1c6752a81416ece61ea828f8"}, "language": "english", "review": "pretty good, now that theres an offline mode", "timestamp_created": 1739873458, "timestamp_updated": 1739873458, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 12, "votes_funny": 7, "weighted_vote_score": "0.582599103450775146", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1682985798", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "187720202", "author": {"steamid": "76561199122976643", "personaname": "Beat Banger Professional", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/KimikoTheTanuki/", "num_games_owned": 476, "num_reviews": 111, "playtime_forever": 1300, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 875, "deck_playtime_at_review": 91, "last_played": 1745960270, "avatar": "98c444043a8df74b7d53d76a6fe95d19e98a8daa"}, "language": "english", "review": "This was Arkane Austin's last game before Microsoft killed them off.\n\nA game that no one wanted to finish.\nA game that Microsoft forced them to release. \n\nThe worst part being that this game could've been amazing. The base is there. Arkane's soul is here, just tainted by corporations forcing crunch and quickly piecing together parts. \nI enjoyed myself playing the game, and I'd say it's worth it to get the game for $7 through Fanatical. \n\nBut man, what a waste of potential.\nMicrosoft, I will never forgive you for killing off this studio along with Tango Gameworks.", "timestamp_created": 1739299644, "timestamp_updated": 1739299644, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 175, "votes_funny": 2, "weighted_vote_score": "0.899843573570251465", "comment_count": 5, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1682985798", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 2, "count": 6}, {"reaction_type": 17, "count": 3}, {"reaction_type": 16, "count": 2}, {"reaction_type": 8, "count": 2}, {"reaction_type": 22, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 18, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "187605427", "author": {"steamid": "76561198269505892", "personaname": "gree", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/smurfblevins/", "num_games_owned": 688, "num_reviews": 86, "playtime_forever": 134, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 107, "last_played": 1739247523, "avatar": "7acdbbf5858aadc299bc418eb8a0b04db42c2b19"}, "language": "english", "review": "As half baked as half baked gets, monumental disaster that caused a once great studio to get shuttered. Shame, really.", "timestamp_created": 1739156843, "timestamp_updated": 1739156843, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.489361703395843506", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1682985798", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "187576813", "author": {"steamid": "76561198276457735", "personaname": "vaulthouston373", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198276457735/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 14, "playtime_forever": 60, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 60, "last_played": 1724011648, "avatar": "a08c3e17f20dfd418af17da6a8900c9e08325fa2"}, "language": "english", "review": "Why the Hell does this thing take up so much space? You are better off playing Left for Dead 1 or 2. Takes up less space and the creator knew how to code.", "timestamp_created": 1739126266, "timestamp_updated": 1739126266, "v